 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? You still remember the basics, which is great. Have you tried speaking with native speakers? Often they can't recognize how much you've improved until you ask. Not annoying at all. Lots of people stop practicing because they believe they'll never sound native. Giving yourself a goal, like being confident during a job interview, can really help. Listen to yourself with recorder, and ask a teacher to look at the tape. Great habit for developed language learners. A journal is perfect for exploring vocabulary and grammar in context.",
